@SneakyThrows
public <T> Mono<T> sendFlexRequest(
    String endpoint,
    HttpMethod method,
    Map<String, String> additionalHeaders,
    Object requestBody,
    Class<T> responseType) {

  log.info(
      new LogBuilder()
          .withField("endpoint", endpoint)
          .withField("method", method.toString())
          .withField("additional headers", additionalHeaders.toString())
          .withMessage("sendflex API request call")
          .toString());

  return webClient
      .method(method)
      .uri(getURI(endpoint))
      .headers(
          httpHeaders -> {
            getDefaultHeaders().forEach(httpHeaders::add);
            if (!additionalHeaders.isEmpty()) {
              additionalHeaders.forEach(httpHeaders::add);
            }
          })
      .bodyValue(requestBody == null ? Mono.empty() : requestBody)
      .retrieve()
      .bodyToMono(responseType)
      .retryWhen(
          retryConfig.createRetry(
              MAX_ATTEMPTS,
              INITIAL_DELAY_SECONDS))
      .onErrorMap(throwable -> handleErrorMap(throwable, endpoint));
}

Why?

We are changing:

.onErrorMap(this::handleErrorMap)

to:

.onErrorMap(throwable -> handleErrorMap(throwable, endpoint))

This allows handleErrorMap() to know that the request is:

/AddressValidation

and therefore only apply the special WARN behavior to this API.


