RetryConfig.java

Your retry logic itself is already correct.

This:

return statusCode >= 500 && statusCode < 600;

means:

400 → don't retry
401 → don't retry
404 → don't retry
500 → retry
502 → retry
503 → retry

So do not change the retry condition.

But change isRetryable().

Current:

public boolean isRetryable(Throwable throwable) {
    if (throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {
        int statusCode = ex.getStatusCode().value();
        log.error(new LogBuilder()
                        .withMessage("Is this request retryable?")
                        .withField("statusCode", statusCode)
                        .toString());
        return statusCode >= 500 && statusCode < 600;
    }
    return true;
}

Replace with:

public boolean isRetryable(Throwable throwable) {
  if (throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {
    int statusCode = ex.getStatusCode().value();
    return statusCode >= 500 && statusCode < 600;
  }

  return true;
}

That's it.

Why?

This existing code:

log.error(...)

is another source of ERROR logging for a 400.

We don't need this log because the actual error logging is handled by SendFlexWebClientService.


